  { p: 'Which philosopher systematised Advaita Vedanta (non-dualism)?', op: ['Ramanuja', 'Madhva', 'Nagarjuna', 'Shankara'], certa: 3, exp: 'Adi Shankara (8th c., according to most historians) commented on the Upanishads, the Gita and the Brahma Sutras.' },
  { p: 'In what language did the Alvars and Nayanars sing their hymns of devotion?', op: ['Sanskrit', 'Pali', 'Tamil', 'Persian'], certa: 2, exp: 'In Tamil, between the 6th and 9th centuries, in the temples of Shiva and Vishnu in the south.' },
  { p: 'Who conquered Sindh for the Umayyad caliphate in 711 – 712?', op: ['Mahmud of Ghazni', 'Muhammad ibn al-Qasim', 'Qutb ud-Din Aibak', 'Babur'], certa: 1, exp: 'Muhammad ibn al-Qasim defeated King Dahir; it was the first lasting Islamic presence in the subcontinent.' },
  { p: 'What work did Al-Biruni write about India, around 1030?', op: ['Kitab al-Hind', 'Arthashastra', 'Natya Shastra', 'Indica'], certa: 0, exp: 'The *Kitab al-Hind* describes the religion, science and customs of the Indians, based on Sanskrit texts.' },
  { p: 'What do Patanjali’s Yoga Sutras (dating debated) say about the practice of yoga?', op: ['They focus on complex physical postures', 'They focus on mental discipline and meditation, with few references to postures', 'They forbid meditation', 'They are a gymnastics manual'], certa: 1, exp: 'Modern postural yoga is above all a creation of the 20th century, with roots in medieval hatha yoga.' },
  { p: 'What happened at Calicut in 1498, according to the Roteiro of Vasco da Gama’s voyage?', op: ['He was expelled by the Zamorin', 'The Portuguese entered a Hindu temple thinking it was a Christian church', 'He met the king of Vijayanagara', 'He visited Nalanda'], certa: 1, exp: 'The account shows how the Portuguese interpreted, on first contact, the religions they met.' }
